WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:03.303 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Voice cracking ]
Our first guest tonight
is an Emmy, Golden Globe,

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:04.437 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Academy Award-nominated
actress.

00:00:04.437 --> 00:00:06.039
You know her best from her roles
in "Unfaithful,"

00:00:06.039 --> 00:00:07.640 size:81% position:41%
"Under the Tuscan Sun"
and "Justice League."

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:10.477
She's currently starring in the
final season of "House of Cards"

00:00:10.477 --> 00:00:14.781
which begins streaming in its
entirety on Netflix this Friday.

00:00:14.781 --> 00:00:15.415 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Let's take a look.

00:00:15.415 --> 00:00:21.087
-Whatever Francis promised
or did is buried with him.

00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:24.691 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-No, I-I know.

00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:27.694 line:92%
We all need to let him go,

00:00:27.694 --> 00:00:32.332 line:92%
start from some kind of scratch.

00:00:32.332 --> 00:00:34.601 line:92%
Though, it must haunt you,

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:37.203 size:78% position:39%
the fact that he died
next to you in bed?

00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:40.907 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Please welcome to the show
Diane Lane, everybody.

00:00:40.907 --> 00:00:43.343 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:43.343 --> 00:00:50.083 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:00:50.083 --> 00:00:56.122 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:00:56.122 --> 00:00:59.993 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thanks so much.
This is so nice of you.

00:00:59.993 --> 00:01:02.562
Oh, that's great.
This is your "I Voted" sticker?

00:01:02.562 --> 00:01:04.898 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, and I wanted to ask you
where I should put it.

00:01:04.898 --> 00:01:06.933
-I would go right there. I would
go in the part that goes --

00:01:06.933 --> 00:01:09.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
-My daughter said so. too.
-Yeah. There you go.

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:10.870 size:75% position:38% line:92%
So you've already...

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:12.205 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:12.205 --> 00:01:13.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's great.
-I'm psyched. I'm psyched.

00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:17.143
-I feel like that's the
undiscovered country that
everybody has to realize,

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:20.513 align:start size:94% position:6%
is you got to vote early
because you avoid the lines,

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:21.514 line:92%
it's such a better scene.

00:01:21.514 --> 00:01:22.615
-Yes!
-And now get it out of the way.

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:25.085
You have nothing to worry about.
-And you have time to read

00:01:25.085 --> 00:01:26.386 align:start size:94% position:6%
all the propositions
and measurements

00:01:26.386 --> 00:01:28.955 align:start size:94% position:6%
and to have your say
in the future.

00:01:28.955 --> 00:01:30.824 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-Yes. All right. Great.

00:01:30.824 --> 00:01:33.393 size:75% position:38%
And, also, thank you
for my cough drops.

00:01:33.393 --> 00:01:35.228 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They were handed to me.
I'm not a sponsor.

00:01:35.228 --> 00:01:37.230 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They were handed to you.
Okay, gotcha.

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:38.465 size:84% position:42% line:92%
So, this is really cool

00:01:38.465 --> 00:01:40.834
that you are on the last season
of "House of Cards."

00:01:40.834 --> 00:01:42.202 line:92%
But obviously this is a show

00:01:42.202 --> 00:01:44.037 align:start size:94% position:6%
that there was a lot of
uncertainty as to what was

00:01:44.037 --> 00:01:46.739
going to happen moving forward
based on things that happened

00:01:46.739 --> 00:01:47.640 line:92%
outside the realm of the show.

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:50.310 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, we had a little more
zeitgeist than we --

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:51.511 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah.
-Than we...

00:01:51.511 --> 00:01:52.846 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-...anticipated.

00:01:52.846 --> 00:01:55.014 align:start size:94% position:6%
Get your hand
caught in the machine.

00:01:55.014 --> 00:01:56.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's what I call that,
when you suddenly

00:01:56.649 --> 00:01:59.652
become part of the hashtags
and movements and headlines.

00:01:59.652 --> 00:02:03.423 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes. Maybe. Yeah. Right at
the beginning of that, really.

00:02:03.423 --> 00:02:05.391 align:start size:94% position:6%
But what was the --
When you showed up --

00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:07.193 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously your first year
was this year.

00:02:07.193 --> 00:02:08.962 align:start size:94% position:6%
What was the tone like
when you arrived?

00:02:08.962 --> 00:02:11.831 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was -- Well, it was
interesting because for me

00:02:11.831 --> 00:02:14.534 align:start size:94% position:6%
I didn't want to be
an interloper.

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:15.602 line:92%
I mean, I'm a fan of the show.

00:02:15.602 --> 00:02:20.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
And to be allowed in,
I had to cram and catch up.

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:23.243 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's sort of
like being a kid

00:02:23.243 --> 00:02:25.478 align:start size:94% position:6%
on the first day of school
in a new school.

00:02:25.478 --> 00:02:28.381 align:start size:94% position:6%
You just want
to seamlessly sneak in

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:31.217
and not draw too much attention
to yourself, you know?

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:34.020 align:start size:94% position:6%
But that was unavoidable,
because Robin and I were like

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:37.524
two cobras hissing at each other
whenever the camera's on.

00:02:37.524 --> 00:02:39.192 align:start size:94% position:6%
So much fun.
-You also --

00:02:39.192 --> 00:02:40.927 align:start size:94% position:6%
One of your co-stars
is Greg Kinnear.

00:02:40.927 --> 00:02:42.629 align:start size:94% position:6%
You guys play
brother and sister.

00:02:42.629 --> 00:02:45.732 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I like you in puberty.
This is adorable.

00:02:45.732 --> 00:02:48.034 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What's that?
-Isn't it great?

00:02:48.034 --> 00:02:50.470 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, it's pretty sexy.
-It's working.

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:52.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. How do I keep it?
-So, Greg Kinnear --

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:55.241 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know what?
I do not want these.

00:02:55.241 --> 00:02:56.709 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.709 --> 00:03:00.346 align:start size:94% position:6%
So you guys are sort of
wealthy brother and sister...

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:00.813 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:03:00.813 --> 00:03:02.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...who are trying
to control politics.

00:03:02.182 --> 00:03:06.119 align:start size:94% position:6%
Very evocative of some people
who are in the news.

00:03:06.119 --> 00:03:07.620 line:92%
Was that a fun thing to play?

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:10.690 size:78% position:39%
-Well, power is fun,
especially for girls.

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:14.494 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. Sure. Yeah.
-We know what to do with it.

00:03:14.494 --> 00:03:16.930 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:19.065 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-No, it was --

00:03:19.065 --> 00:03:20.466 line:92%
That seems to me what will be

00:03:20.466 --> 00:03:22.602 align:start size:94% position:6%
the most interesting dynamic
of this season.

00:03:22.602 --> 00:03:24.804 line:92%
-Yes, and I made a few jokes

00:03:24.804 --> 00:03:26.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
about voting for Robin
for president.

00:03:26.339 --> 00:03:28.942 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, Claire frightens me,
but Robin's great.

00:03:28.942 --> 00:03:30.210 line:92%
-Yeah, well, I want to ask this

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:32.912
because you're also in Matthew
Weiner's show, "The Romanoffs."

00:03:32.912 --> 00:03:36.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
-All in one week. 18 months
of my life in one week.

00:03:36.649 --> 00:03:38.718 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
Pretty amazing.

00:03:38.718 --> 00:03:41.120 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You are primarily known
for film work,

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:42.622 align:start size:94% position:6%
but it does seem
in recent years,

00:03:42.622 --> 00:03:45.158 align:start size:94% position:6%
a lot of film actors have
found their way to television.

00:03:45.158 --> 00:03:46.392 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is it just the quality
of the work?

00:03:46.392 --> 00:03:50.830
-Well, I think it's good
to walk through the open doors.

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:52.298 align:start size:94% position:6%
And there's
a lot more opportunity

00:03:52.298 --> 00:03:53.299 align:start size:94% position:6%
in terms of the quality
of writing

00:03:53.299 --> 00:03:56.502
and the diversity of experience
that women are allowed to have

00:03:56.502 --> 00:03:57.570 size:75% position:38% line:92%
on the small screen.

00:03:57.570 --> 00:04:02.175 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know,
it's nice to be invited.

00:04:02.175 --> 00:04:04.077 align:start size:94% position:6%
And such talented people.
My gosh.

00:04:04.077 --> 00:04:07.447
I mean, if you're going to
start in television, go big.

00:04:07.447 --> 00:04:09.616 size:75% position:38%
I mean, I don't even
call it television.

00:04:09.616 --> 00:04:11.918 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because it's --
Once Netflix introduced

00:04:11.918 --> 00:04:13.586 align:start size:94% position:6%
binging through
"House of Cards,"

00:04:13.586 --> 00:04:15.188 align:start size:94% position:6%
it was a game changer
for everybody.

00:04:15.188 --> 00:04:18.858
And so now with Matt Weiner's
new show, "The Romanoffs,"

00:04:18.858 --> 00:04:20.560 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's appointment
television again.

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:22.428 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-So we're going retro.

00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:23.863 line:92%
-Right, 'cause it is. Yeah.

00:04:23.863 --> 00:04:25.365 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, to go back to that,
it's fun.

00:04:25.365 --> 00:04:29.168
-"The Romanoffs" episode you're
in takes place in New York.

00:04:29.168 --> 00:04:30.003 size:81% position:41% line:92%
You used to live here.

00:04:30.003 --> 00:04:32.038
-Yeah, I grew up here.
Born and raised and bred.

00:04:32.038 --> 00:04:33.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You grew up here,
born and raised.

00:04:33.873 --> 00:04:35.375 align:start size:94% position:6%
-PS 59.
-PS 59. Wow.

00:04:35.375 --> 00:04:39.012 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah.
-And so how has it changed?

00:04:39.012 --> 00:04:39.712 line:92%
Like, when you come back,

00:04:39.712 --> 00:04:41.414 align:start size:94% position:6%
are you blown away
by how different it is?

00:04:41.414 --> 00:04:44.484
-Oh, yeah.
My school is now a Whole Foods.

00:04:44.484 --> 00:04:44.917 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Wow.

00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:47.654
-My first kiss was in the
produce section, I guess.

00:04:47.654 --> 00:04:51.491 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now, well -- Yeah, New York
has changed a lot.

00:04:51.491 --> 00:04:53.126 size:84% position:42%
There's a book I wanted
to get for you today

00:04:53.126 --> 00:04:55.995
because I knew I was going to
want to mention this to you.

00:04:55.995 --> 00:04:59.766
There's a book by E.B. White
called "This Is New York."

00:04:59.766 --> 00:05:00.967 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you have it?
-I don't. No.

00:05:00.967 --> 00:05:03.469 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's mandatory reading
for us New Yorkers

00:05:03.469 --> 00:05:06.906 align:start size:94% position:6%
because New York betrays
its most devoted, loyal lovers

00:05:06.906 --> 00:05:11.144 align:start size:94% position:6%
of the city because
it can't help but change.

00:05:11.144 --> 00:05:13.980 align:start size:94% position:6%
It must change.
And we all feel --

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:15.848 align:start size:94% position:6%
This book was written
70 years ago, by the way,

00:05:15.848 --> 00:05:19.052 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's very timeless
and still true.

00:05:19.052 --> 00:05:21.020 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It changes quickly.
-It must.

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:24.023 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, so, growing up here,
on Halloween, I have to ask --

00:05:24.023 --> 00:05:25.692 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because I grew up
in the suburbs.

00:05:25.692 --> 00:05:29.829
My parents would have to drive
me in a car from house to house.

00:05:29.829 --> 00:05:30.830 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Ohh! You had trees.
-Yeah.

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:32.231 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, trick-or-treating
was a drag.

00:05:32.231 --> 00:05:35.702 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Lucky. That was the fantasy
of every city kid.

00:05:35.702 --> 00:05:37.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
It really is not that great.

00:05:37.103 --> 00:05:40.073
-We would just go to the
richest girl that we could find

00:05:40.073 --> 00:05:41.641 line:92%
and be her friend for Halloween

00:05:41.641 --> 00:05:45.278
and say, "Can we go to your
building for trick-or-treat?"

00:05:45.278 --> 00:05:47.246 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we'd just go
to the top floor

00:05:47.246 --> 00:05:48.715 align:start size:94% position:6%
and work our way
down the stairwell and...

00:05:48.715 --> 00:05:51.484 align:start size:94% position:6%
-See, that's so much more fun
than what I had to do.

00:05:51.484 --> 00:05:54.387
-...come out with two years'
worth of candy in one building.

00:05:54.387 --> 00:05:55.888 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I would take
like four hours,

00:05:55.888 --> 00:05:59.058 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I would get,
like, a Kit-Kat.

00:05:59.058 --> 00:06:00.426 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You earned it.
-I did. I earned it.

00:06:00.426 --> 00:06:03.162
-What was your favorite costume?
-What was my favorite costume?

00:06:03.162 --> 00:06:05.131 align:start size:94% position:6%
I actually remember
when I was really young,

00:06:05.131 --> 00:06:08.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said that I wanted to dress
like a pile of trash.

00:06:08.368 --> 00:06:10.737 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-That's different.

00:06:10.737 --> 00:06:11.938 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And my dad
did this excellent --

00:06:11.938 --> 00:06:14.774
made me an excellent costume,
and I still think to this day

00:06:14.774 --> 00:06:16.642 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's the best costume I had.
Did you have a favorite?

00:06:16.642 --> 00:06:19.278
-Well, I got to have my revenge
on my daughter

00:06:19.278 --> 00:06:20.146 size:78% position:39% line:92%
when it was her turn.

00:06:20.146 --> 00:06:22.782 align:start size:94% position:6%
I got to make her
the costume I always wanted,

00:06:22.782 --> 00:06:23.783 align:start size:94% position:6%
which was to be a mermaid.
-Oh, wow.

00:06:23.783 --> 00:06:26.619
-Which is tricky, 'cause you
have to kind of waddle around.

00:06:26.619 --> 00:06:29.789
-Yeah.
-You have to really be invested.

00:06:29.789 --> 00:06:31.991 line:92%
-How does it actually work?

00:06:31.991 --> 00:06:33.593 align:start size:94% position:6%
You just put the two feet
out of the bottom?

00:06:33.593 --> 00:06:35.928
-You make a little hole for your
feet in the tail, kind of.

00:06:35.928 --> 00:06:39.198 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It feels like you wanted her
to get less candy.

00:06:39.198 --> 00:06:40.199 line:92%
That feels like the plan.

00:06:40.199 --> 00:06:41.601 size:75% position:38%
-I wanted to be able
to keep up with her.

00:06:41.601 --> 00:06:44.637 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Just slow her down enough.
-Speedy McGee.

